Animation is the technique of creating the illusion of motion by displaying a sequence of images
(frames) in rapid succession. In computer graphics, animation is achieved by continuously updating
the position, shape, or properties of objects over time.
1. glTranslatef()
12. Purpose: Used to move (translate) an object in 3D space.
13. Syntax: glTranslatef(x, y, z);

